WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.760
As the horror genre's reigning Final Girl,&nbsp;
Laurie Strode, played by Jamie Lee Curtis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.800
exceeds her reputation in the 2018 sequel,&nbsp;
"Halloween." Despite the self-inflicted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:16.240
isolation of her militaristic lifestyle and the&nbsp;
resulting strained relationships with her family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.400
Strode is ready for the inevitable&nbsp;
return of Michael Myers.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:25.760
"Halloween" is the first installment in a trilogy&nbsp;
directed by David Gordon Green. The films are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:31.840
direct sequels to the original 1978 film of the&nbsp;
same name directed by John Carpenter. The film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:38.640
became the highest-grossing entry in the Halloween&nbsp;
franchise, making over $250 million worldwide.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.520
According to Entertainment Weekly, co-writer Danny&nbsp;
McBride said they were eager to shoot a sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:49.920
but wanted to make sure audiences were on board&nbsp;
first. "Halloween" is certified fresh on Rotten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:55.520
Tomatoes, with many critics and fans agreeing&nbsp;
that it's a welcome change for the franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.880
Now, the much-anticipated&nbsp;
sequel, "Halloween Kills,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:04.240
is officially on the horizon, and here’s&nbsp;
everything we know about the film so far.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:10.640
The initial release date of "Halloween Kills"&nbsp;
was October 16, 2020, but a July 2020 statement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:15.360
from Green and Carpenter revealed that the&nbsp;
film was delayed because of the pandemic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.600
Not dissimilar to many other films that&nbsp;
were scheduled to be released in 2020.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.640
"If we release it in October&nbsp;
of this year as planned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:28.080
we have to face the reality that the film would be&nbsp;
consumed in a compromised theatrical experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:33.360
After weighing our options, we have chosen to&nbsp;
push the film's theatrical release by one year."

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.720
Now, nearly one year later, "Halloween Kills"&nbsp;
is scheduled to premiere at the 17th Venice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:44.000
International Film Festival on September 8.&nbsp;
It’ll be hitting U.S. theaters on October 15.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:50.080
Additionally, the release date for "Halloween&nbsp;
Ends" is set for October 14, 2022, meaning we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:55.200
shouldn't have to endure such a brutal wait&nbsp;
time before seeing the trilogy's final entry.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:00.880
Of course, Jamie Lee Curtis will be reprising&nbsp;
her iconic role as Laurie Strode, the tormented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:05.680
babysitter-turned-fighter. The other Strode women&nbsp;
will be returning as well. Judy Greer is back as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.720
Laurie's estranged daughter, Karen, and Andi&nbsp;
Matichak is back as Karen's daughter, Allyson.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:14.960
Additionally, Michael Myers will be portrayed&nbsp;
by Nick Castle and James Jude Courtney again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:19.920
Will Patton and Jibrail Nantambu will also be&nbsp;
reprising their roles from the previous film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:24.960
While "Halloween Kills" is naturally pulling&nbsp;
from characters introduced in the 2018 film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:28.720
it's also bringing back&nbsp;
characters from the 1978 version.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.400
The young children Laurie babysat in&nbsp;
the original are all grown up now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:37.120
Tommy Doyle will be portrayed by Anthony Michael&nbsp;
Hall, while Kyle Richards is reprising her role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:40.960
as Lindsey Wallace. Nancy Stephens is&nbsp;
reprising her role as Marion Chambers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.800
a retired nurse. Charles Cyphers is&nbsp;
reprising his role as Leigh Brackett,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:48.080
the former Haddonfield sheriff&nbsp;
whose daughter was killed by Myers.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.760
In an interview with Empire,&nbsp;
Green and McBride explained that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.320
"Halloween Kills" picks up directly where the&nbsp;
previous film ended. However, while the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:01.280
film focused on Laurie's life 40 years after&nbsp;
surviving a brutal killing spree. Green said,

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:05.360
"This is more about the unravelling&nbsp;
of a community into chaos."

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:11.680
The 2018 film ends with Michael Myers trapped and&nbsp;
left for dead in Laurie's flame-engulfed home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:17.760
but as fans know, the Captain Kirk-Masked&nbsp;
killer doesn't go down easily. Or at all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.360
The "Halloween Kills" trailer shows&nbsp;
Myers walking out the front door&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:26.400
and attacking the firefighters before resuming&nbsp;
his reign of terror on the small Midwestern town.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:31.360
As Myers leaves a trail of bodies leading&nbsp;
to his childhood home where it all began,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:36.080
the Haddonfield residents rally together to&nbsp;
hunt down the obsessive killer. Laurie leaves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:41.120
the hospital where she's recovering from&nbsp;
a stab wound and makes a bold declaration.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.080
"Evil dies tonight."

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.000
McBride explained to Empire,

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:51.520
"Events in the film bring together a lot of&nbsp;
characters who were in the 1978 film who we didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:58.240
see last time. They gather to try, once and for&nbsp;
all, to take down Michael, to stop this madman."

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:02.400
It's unlikely that Myers will be defeated&nbsp;
in "Halloween Kills," especially considering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:06.640
that there's one more film to come in&nbsp;
the trilogy, but anything’s possible.

